## Documentation (check for API usage and tutorials)
- None found specifically for browser + pptx agent, but general docs may exist in docs/ (not searched here)

## Examples (MOST IMPORTANT)
- examples/usecases/pptx_toolkit_usecase/app_pptx.py
  - Streamlit app example showing usage of PPTXToolkit and ChatAgent to generate PowerPoint slides from a topic prompt.
  - Shows how to create a ChatAgent with OpenAI GPT-4o model, generate structured JSON for slides, and create PPTX files.
- examples/usecases/cloudfare_mcp_camel/app.py
  - Streamlit app example showing usage of ChatAgent with MCPToolkit including browser capabilities.
  - Demonstrates creating an agent with browser tools to fetch and analyze web pages.
- examples/agents/create_chat_agent.py
  - Shows multiple ways to create ChatAgent instances with different model configurations.
  - Useful for understanding agent creation patterns.

## Implementation
- camel/toolkits/browser_toolkit.py
  - Implements BrowserToolkit class wrapping a BaseBrowser for web browsing and interaction.
  - Provides methods for browsing URLs, observing and acting on web pages, and integrating with ChatAgent.
- camel/toolkits/pptx_toolkit.py
  - Implements PPTXToolkit class for creating PowerPoint presentations programmatically.
  - Provides methods to create presentations from structured JSON content.
- camel/toolkits/__init__.py
  - Exports BrowserToolkit and PPTXToolkit among many other toolkits.

## Configuration/Types
- camel/types/enums.py (not searched here but known location)
  - Defines ModelPlatformType and ModelType enums used for model selection in agents.

Summary:
- For creating an agent with browser and PPT tools, use BrowserToolkit and PPTXToolkit implementations.
- The example in examples/usecases/pptx_toolkit_usecase/app_pptx.py shows how to create a ChatAgent and use PPTXToolkit to generate slides.
- The example in examples/usecases/cloudfare_mcp_camel/app.py shows how to create a ChatAgent with browser tools.
- Use examples/agents/create_chat_agent.py for agent creation patterns.

These files provide the core components and usage patterns needed to create the requested agent script.
